{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And there shall not be like Korah.</b> So that there shall not be like Korah." "<b>As YHWH spoke by the hand of Moses to him.</b> Like 'upon him' — concerning Aaron He spoke to Moses, that he and his sons shall be priests; therefore ״No stranger who is not of the seed of Aaron shall draw near״ etc. And so every li, lo, and lahem adjacent to a speaking — their resolution is like 'upon.' And its midrash — concerning Korah. And what is ״by the hand of Moses״ and it does not write ״to Moses״? An allusion to those who dispute the priesthood — they are stricken with tzara'at as Moses was stricken in his hand, as it says ״וַיּוֹצִאָהּ וְהִנֵּה יָדוֹ מְצֹרַעַת כַּשָּׁלֶג״ (Exodus 4), and accordingly Uzziah was stricken with tzara'at (II Chronicles 26)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:24.109313686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}